{
  "challenge": "JAVA-005",
  "task": "Shift each ASCII letter around its alphabet by offset positions, preserving case.\n\nImplement `Solution.shift(String text, int offset)`. Wrap z to a and Z to A. Negative offsets shift backward. Leave spaces, digits and punctuation unchanged. Input has at most 200 ASCII characters; offset is -10000..10000. Empty input returns an empty string.\n\n## Examples\n\nInput: `[\"Az-9!\", 1]` → output: `\"Ba-9!\"`.\nInput: `[\"abc\", -1]` → output: `\"zab\"`.\n",
  "language": "java",
  "file": "Solution.java",
  "starter": "// TODO: implement the task.\npublic class Solution {\n    public static String shift(String text, int offset) { return text; }\n}\n",
  "entrypoint": "shift",
  "parameters": [
    "text",
    "offset"
  ],
  "adapter": "final class Adapter {\n    static Object call(Json args) {\n        return Solution.shift(args.at(0).asString(), args.at(1).asInt());\n    }\n}\n",
